## SQ-CMP-05 | TNT item in fire, fireproof item in lava
@group A
@commands Same boot: throw a TNT-tagged item into fire (an item burn rule with shrapnel); throw a fireproof item into lava
@pass Blast plus shrapnel as before; fireproof item survives
@fails `BurnBursts` handler not registered by the shrapnel side
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-5, 2026-11-18): the {H} home marker came from a lost setup row; fixed superflat spot
> forceload add 200 200 232 232
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome] run summon minecraft:marker 200 -60 200 {Tags:["cmphome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome,limit=1] Pos
capture H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {H1+20} {H3+20}
sleep 5
# items of the same kind merge: clear earlier test items first
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x={H1+22},y={H2},z={H3+20},distance=..30]
> setblock {H1+20} {H2-1} {H3+20} minecraft:netherrack
> setblock {H1+20} {H2} {H3+20} minecraft:fire
> setblock {H1+24} {H2-1} {H3+20} minecraft:stone
> setblock {H1+24} {H2} {H3+20} minecraft:lava
> summon minecraft:item {H1+20} {H2+1} {H3+20} {Item:{id:"minecraft:tnt",Count:1b},Tags:["cmp_tnt2"]}
> summon minecraft:item {H1+24} {H2+1} {H3+20} {Item:{id:"minecraft:netherite_ingot",Count:1b},Tags:["cmp_fp2"]}
sleep 15
> execute if block {H1+20} {H2} {H3+20} minecraft:fire run say CMP fire still burning
> execute unless entity @e[type=item,tag=cmp_tnt2] run say CMP tnt item burned
> execute if entity @e[type=item,tag=cmp_fp2] run say CMP fireproof item survived
expect CMP tnt item burned
expect CMP fireproof item survived
shell grep -iE "shrapnel|burnExplode|BurnBursts" logs/latest.log | tail -3 | cut -c1-200
look the blast itself is not visible on a console; the TNT item is consumed and the netherite stays

## SQ-CMP-06 | weathered cardboard box, monster box loot, physics tags
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/give` a weathered cardboard box and place it; `/loot` the monster box reward table; check `#creativeengineering:...` physics tags with `/dumptags`
@pass Block and item exist (`creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box`); loot table resolves; physics tags present
@fails Startup `decor_blocks.js` or jar data paths
@from batches/r1101/cs2_boot2.qb
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-5, 2026-11-18; ids creativecompat: since the 2026-11-09 move): the {H} home marker came from a lost setup row; fixed superflat spot
> forceload add 200 200 232 232
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome] run summon minecraft:marker 200 -60 200 {Tags:["cmphome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cmphome,limit=1] Pos
capture H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> execute unless entity qa run pbot spawn qa {H1} {H2} {H3} minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> setblock {H1+8} {H2} {H3} creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box
> execute if block {H1+8} {H2} {H3} creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box run say CMP box placed
> give qa creativecompat:weathered_cardboard_box
> loot give qa loot creativecompat:misc/monster_box_reward
expect CMP box placed
reject Unknown (block|item)|Unknown loot table
> dumptags
waitlog (dumptags|tags).*(done|written|wrote) 300
shell python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/tags/item_tags_by_item.json'));print({k:len(v) for k,v in d.items() if 'cardboard' in k})" 2>&1 | cut -c1-300; ls kubejs/exported/tags/ | head
look block, item and loot resolve; physics tags present

